{
  "$comment": [
    "PHASE 106 — Journal taxonomy for the multilingual engineering corpus.",
    "",
    "Categories and tags referenced by content/journal/articles/*/article.json are",
    "declared HERE and upserted by scripts/journal/import-articles.mjs. The",
    "importer refuses to invent a category or tag it has not been shown, so a typo",
    "in an article manifest is a validation error rather than a silently created",
    "duplicate taxonomy row.",
    "",
    "Category slugs deliberately reuse the ones the Journal already ships (see",
    "src/lib/articles/mock-data.ts MOCK_CATEGORIES) so imported content lands in",
    "the existing navigation instead of creating a parallel set. `nameDe` is new in",
    "Phase 106; `sortOrder` and `color` match the established values.",
    "",
    "TAG NAMES ARE NOT TRANSLATED WHEN THEY ARE PROTOCOL OR PRODUCT NAMES.",
    "PROFINET, OPC UA and IEC 61131-3 are the same string in every language;",
    "inventing a Persian or German 'translation' for a standard designation would",
    "be wrong, not helpful. nameFa is populated only where a genuine Persian term",
    "exists."
  ],
